# SCR-M: screening point for a slice of Fable's profile M, CDC (streams-cost
# report 2026-10-24 §4.1), on the launch posture: one shared-cell server
# (compute-1g.env + shared-cell.env: one shard, fleet off, an 8 MiB tail ring
# (unset with SERVER_ENV_EXTRA=-TAIL_RING_BYTES),
# 32/16 MiB caches), s3lite at 20 ms. About 20-25 minutes:
#
#   10 streams; batched appends of 100 x 1 KiB JSON records under one of 64
#   routing keys per request, at M_RATE (3) req/s, open-loop Poisson: a
#   quarter of M's 12.1 req/s (300 records/s, ~26 GB/day);
#   two consumer groups (pull max 100, settle each, waiting up to 20 s as
#   the SDK's consumers do): a pull leases one key's run, here one
#   request's 100 records;
#   a long-poll tail per stream. A read names one routing key (without one
#   it reads only unkeyed records), so each stream's tail follows key k0:
#   10 connections, as M's, delivering ~1/64 of the records.
#
# M is a whole-cell tenant (Fable's model gives it 4.4 cells of pull CPU),
# so this point gives its one project the whole cell's admission, before
# the caller's SERVER_ENV_EXTRA (which can undo it): PROJECT_SHARE_K=1 and
# PROJECT_MEMORY_PRESSURE_BYTES=268435456 (the eight 32 MiB lines of k = 8,
# = MAX_UNABSORBED_BYTES_PER_SHARD). At shared-cell.env's k = 8 one project
# may append 257,500 B/s with a one-second burst, so M is refused (429) at
# any rate above about one 100 KiB request a second; and its 20 concurrent
# pulls held the 32 MiB project memory line (a 60 s smoke at 3 req/s with
# 1 s pull waits: 79 answers 429 project_memory_pressure, 7 to appends and
# 72 to pulls). Both are admission bounds, not the write or read path the
# point prices.
#
# Load LOAD_SECS (780), then a short quiescence (240 s quiet in 60 s
# windows, given up after 720 s: the deferred window is a lower bound on
# history work), then 60 s of idle tail. SCR_SMOKE=1 shortens it to about
# 6 minutes (60 s of load). The rig sets QUIESCE_* and IDLE_SECS before it
# reads a point, so this point sets them plainly; LOAD_SECS, M_RATE and
# SCR_SMOKE come from the caller.
#
# Verdict counts (counts.py RUN; a pair: counts.py --compare REF CAND):
# window `to_quiesced` (and `phases 2-5`, the load alone): shard/sst/get
# (pull and tail store reads: E2), hist/sst/put and the put_bytes of the
# deferred window (history compaction fan-in), shard/wal/put with
# pump_flushes, class_a, class_b, and streams-1's cpu_s (indicative only on
# this host).
POINT_NAME=SCR-M
POSTURE=launch
S3LITE_LATENCY_MS=20
SERVERS=1
SERVER_ENV_EXTRA="PROJECT_SHARE_K=1 PROJECT_MEMORY_PRESSURE_BYTES=268435456${SERVER_ENV_EXTRA:+ $SERVER_ENV_EXTRA}"
M_RATE=${M_RATE:-3}
if [ "${SCR_SMOKE:-0}" = 1 ]; then
  POINT_NAME=SCR-M-smoke
  LOAD_SECS=${LOAD_SECS:-60}
  QUIESCE_MIN_SECS=60
  QUIESCE_WINDOW_SECS=20
  QUIESCE_MAX_SECS=240
  IDLE_SECS=20
  USAGE_WAIT_SECS=120
else
  LOAD_SECS=${LOAD_SECS:-780}
  QUIESCE_MIN_SECS=240
  QUIESCE_WINDOW_SECS=60
  QUIESCE_MAX_SECS=720
  IDLE_SECS=60
fi
PHASES="
setup --streams 10 --prefix scr/m
group --streams 10 --prefix scr/m --group cdc-a --pull 100 --consumers 1 --settle every --wait-ms 20000 --duration $LOAD_SECS &
group --streams 10 --prefix scr/m --group cdc-b --pull 100 --consumers 1 --settle every --wait-ms 20000 --duration $LOAD_SECS &
tail --streams 10 --prefix scr/m --routing-keys 1 --via long-poll --readers 1 --duration $LOAD_SECS &
produce --streams 10 --prefix scr/m --rate $M_RATE --records 100 --record-bytes 1024 --payload corpus --routing-keys 64 --duration $LOAD_SECS --seed 51
"
QUIESCE=1
